{"id": "EUVD-2026-108756", "enisaUuid": "303b9f87-5d13-38b5-bb38-8008f80fcd69", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: free iov when btrfs_uring_read_extent() fails\n\nAfter btrfs_uring_read_extent(), the caller always jumped to out_acct.\nThat skips kfree(data->iov), which is only correct for -EIOCBQUEUED\nwhere the deferred path owns the iov. On failure, fall through to\nout_free instead.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a3addbdc5ad1fd80541a6a4ff4e06cd1331530a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/578ef517142420cf9d36b364ad4b3490b85469fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8ea92830b3e0e163d4e829bdcb17ca83c0f951c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98962"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "045e7beb-ec3b-3ce4-8eda-a2627815a5d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34310c442e175f286b4c06ab5caa4e0b267ea31c <a8ea92830b3e0e163d4e829bdcb17ca83c0f951c"}, {"id": "47df8dee-48e7-3eb6-a996-2fc7276ece27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "8c0d30ae-4fd6-3669-a91f-aa62539c30aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34310c442e175f286b4c06ab5caa4e0b267ea31c <7a3addbdc5ad1fd80541a6a4ff4e06cd1331530a"}, {"id": "b4315dbd-b965-3803-a69a-050fee889b7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bcde2a60-e367-3a06-bc80-03796bc46774", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "e82f753e-dc7a-337d-a0c9-2049dd3514be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "fb70528b-ed5f-3bf7-a9c8-ddd62f3bd0bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"